        "original_id": "7bee93ba-11b6-5f1c-b5ea-c4f07a7c8bb8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang, Heavyweights, The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again, The Shaggy D.A., The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh, The Fox and the Hound\n- People: Bill Bixby, Steven Brill, Judd Apatow, Buddy Baker, Paul J. Smith\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Topics: California Gold Rush, film scoring\n\nFacts:\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang follows slick gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is tricked into caring for orphans who strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- Buddy Baker and Paul J. Smith scored many Disney films, including The Apple Dumpling Gang in 1975.\n- Buddy Baker and Paul J. Smith also scored The Shaggy D.A. in 1976 and The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh in 1977.\n- Buddy Baker and Paul J. Smith scored The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again in 1979 and The Fox and the Hound in 1981.\n- Heavyweights is a 1995 American comedy-drama film directed by Steven Brill and written by Steven Brill with Judd Apatow.\n- Buddy Baker, born Norman Dale Baker, was an American composer who lived from January 4, 1918 to July 26, 2002.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
